The 'hooks' folder contains reusable React hooks that manage specific functionalities and state across the game client application, such as UI management, game data handling, and connection logic. Each hook encapsulates distinct responsibilities like chat logging, equipment tracking, terminal behavior, and plugin management, promoting modularity and code reuse throughout the project. These hooks integrate seamlessly with the application's layout and data flow, providing consistent and reactive state management for both user interface and game mechanics.

useAccountModal.ts Load gotcha: the cloud snapshot and the local summary are read BEFORE window.confirm and applied AFTER it, with no re-fetch in between. The confirm is synchronous and blocks the page, but a user who leaves it open for a long time and then accepts applies a stale snapshot (another device may have saved meanwhile). Acceptable today because Load only replaces from what the user was shown; if the confirm ever becomes an async dialog, re-fetch after it and re-plan instead of reusing the snapshot.

Testing useAccountModal: jsdom cannot reload the page, so useAccountModal.test.tsx stubs window.setTimeout and asserts the 3000 ms reload was SCHEDULED rather than performed; window.confirm is stubbed per test. A new Load/Save path needs its own case there, because the apply step runs only after the confirm.

useCharData compares each packet with the previous state (sameFields) and keeps the old object when nothing changed, so an unchanged char_data packet does not re-render HUD consumers; charDataStore is still updated on every packet. Tests count COMMITTED renders (React may call a component once more before bailing out).

useOpponentStatus is mounted once per HUD consumer (classic StatusBlock, CompactVitalsRow, CompactWidgetSlot), so its staleness clock (setNow every 200 ms) runs only while an enemy line is inside ENEMY_STALE_MS and clears itself when stale; an always-on clock re-rendered every enemy bar 5x/s while idle. Its ts/label/pct handling for event:fighting:opponent is unchanged, and useOpponentStatus.test.ts counts renders to guard the idle case.
